 services, merchant services, international banking, correspondent banking, credit card services, and other banking services. This segment also provides securities brokerage services through an arrangement with a third party broker-dealer. The WM&T segment engages in the provision of investment management, financial and retirement planning, and trust and estate services, as well as retirement plan management for businesses and corporations. The company was founded in 1904 and is headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James A. Hillebrand | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $313K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $121K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Stock Yards Bancorp, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.5B market cap on $397M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $154M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 39 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 7.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Stock Yards Bancorp (SYBT) Posted Stronger Earnings, Is The Stock Fully Priced?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-sybt/s